# VaApps R2 Index Architecture | Primary Sources of Truth (Critical)

Three JSON files on Cloudflare R2 are the **authoritative runtime sources** for the entire Whitecardopedia + ValeVision3D platform. They are **machine-generated** by the sync pipeline — never edited by hand and never duplicated in application code.

---

## ⚠️ WHY R2-FIRST LOADING IS CRITICAL — NO GH PUSH FOR PROJECTS

**The whole reason these files live on R2 is so that adding/enabling a project goes live WITHOUT a GitHub Pages push or deploy wait.** Both apps fetch the R2 master config + master index FIRST (cache-busted); the GitHub Pages copies are **fallback only**, used solely when an R2 fetch fails.

- **R2 = live runtime source. GitHub Pages = fallback only.** A project synced by the ValeVision Cloud Sync plugin must appear in seconds with zero git activity.
- **NEVER add logic that requires a GH push to make a project visible or loadable.** If a feature depends on index data, read it from the R2-fetched objects (forwarded onto each project object by the loaders) — not from a committed local copy.
- **NEVER weaken the R2-first fetch order** in either app's project loader. That regression is exactly what produces "synced successfully but the app doesn't show it until I push to GH".
- **Code vs data:** only **app code** (JS/CSS/HTML) changes need a GH push (and, for the PWA, a `PWA_SW_VERSION_TOKEN` bump). **Project/data additions never need a push** — that is the contract this architecture guarantees.

---

## The Three Index Files

### 1. Master App Config Mirror
**Purpose:** Real-time mirror of the master application config. The app fetches this first (cache-busted) so project additions go live without a GitHub Pages push and deploy wait.

| Source | URL |
|--------|-----|
| R2 (primary, real-time) | `https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/VaApps/Index/Na__AppData__MasterConfig__Main.json` |
| GH Pages (fallback) | `02__Src__AppModules/03__AppData/Na__AppData__MasterConfig__Main.json` (Whitecardopedia) |

Contains: project folder list with `enabled` flags, asset URL bases, index URL pointers.

---

### 2. Build Version Manifest
**Purpose:** Monotonically increasing Unix timestamp written after every sync. The app reads this on load (cache-busted) to detect when new images have been synced and evicts the `wpwa-thumbs-*` Service Worker cache bucket automatically — no manual SW version bump needed.

| Source | URL |
|--------|-----|
| R2 (only) | `https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/VaApps/Index/Na__BuildVersion__Manifest__.json` |

Schema: `{ "buildVersion": <unix_timestamp>, "buildDate": "DD-MMM-YYYY at HH:MM", "lastProject": "<name>" }`

---

### 3. Master Project Index
**Purpose:** Authoritative per-project asset location table. Tells the loader whether each project's `project.json` and images live on R2 or GH Pages, and carries audit flags (`hasGlb_R2`, `hasImages_R2`, `imageCount`) that drive UI decisions (carousel gate, 3D badge, etc.).

| Source | URL |
|--------|-----|
| R2 (primary) | `https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/VaApps/Index/Na__MasterIndex__ProjectLocations__.json` |
| GH Pages (fallback) | `02__Src__AppModules/03__AppData/Na__MasterIndex__ProjectLocations__.json` (Whitecardopedia) |

Per-project entry schema:
```json
{
  "folderId"        : "2026/63592__Bressard-Kayode",
  "year"            : "2026",
  "projectCode"     : "63592",
  "name"            : "Bressard-Kayode",
  "enabled"         : true,
  "assetHome"       : "r2",
  "hasProjectJson_R2" : true,
  "hasImages_R2"    : true,
  "hasThumbnails_R2": true,
  "hasGlb_R2"       : true,
  "imageCount"      : 4,
  "lastSynced"      : "25-Jun-2026 at 16:41"
}
```

---

## Who Writes These Files

These files are written **exclusively** by the Python sync pipeline, triggered either by the **ValeVision Cloud Sync SketchUp plugin** or by running the scripts manually.

### Build Scripts (relative to `WebApps/Whitecardopedia/`)

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `Tools__DevUtils/AutomationUtil__SyncSingleProject__ToCloudAndWeb__Main__.py` | **Primary orchestrator** — uploads images, GLBs, thumbnails; rebuilds `project.json`; upserts master index; writes build manifest; mirrors master config to R2 |
| `Tools__DevUtils/AutomationUtil__R2Common__Lib__.py` | **Shared R2 library** — boto3 client, HEAD/list/upload, master index read/upsert/write |
| `Tools__DevUtils/AutomationUtil__AuditAndBackfillR2__ProjectJsonAndImages__Main__.py` | Dry-run/apply audit for missing R2 assets; rebuilds index after apply |
| `Tools__DevUtils/AutomationUtil__BuildCloudflareBucket__WhitecardopediaProjects__Main__.py` | Bulk upload tool; regenerates master index |

---

## Rules for Agents — ALWAYS Follow

- **NEVER manually edit** `Na__MasterIndex__ProjectLocations__.json`, `Na__AppData__MasterConfig__Main.json` (R2 mirror), or `Na__BuildVersion__Manifest__.json`. They are generated output.
- **NEVER duplicate** index data (e.g. `hasGlb_R2`, `imageCount`, `assetHome`) by hardcoding it in JS/JSX. Read it through `Na__AppData__ProjectLoader.js` which forwards index fields onto each project object.
- **NEVER add logic** that fetches these index files independently in new modules. The `ProjectLoader` is the single consumer; build on the fields it exposes (`project.hasGlb_R2`, `project.r2BasePath`, etc.).
- **NEVER hardcode CDN base URLs** (`https://cdn.noble-architecture.com/VaApps/...`) in application code. They are sourced from `Na__AppData__MasterConfig__Main.json` → `Na__AssetUrls__R2Base`.
- If a project's UI behaviour must depend on index data, add the field forwarding in `loadProjectData()` inside `Na__AppData__ProjectLoader.js` and consume `project.<field>` in the component — exactly as `hasGlb_R2` was added.
